  "answer": "This looks like a previously reported problem: Command Palette stays on the desktop as an invisible or lingering window after being dismissed. In #42082 the maintainers traced it to a DWM cloaking failure, which was caused by another app interfering with window handling. In that case it was MyDockFinder's custom window animations. Check whether you run a dock, taskbar replacement, or window-animation/customization tool. Try disabling its window animations or exiting it completely, then see if Command Palette hides properly. The maintainers also said a change making Command Palette resistant to this interference was prepared, so update PowerToys to the latest version. If the problem persists with no such tool running, reply with details of your setup and any similar utilities so the maintainers can investigate."
